<p>Safe transit is achieved through GPS-monitored vehicles equipped with shock indicators and air-ride suspension. The truck is loaded in a weight-balanced configuration, with heavy items anchored to the floor and fragile goods placed in upper compartments. En-route, the driver maintains a constant 60 km/h speed on highways, avoiding sharp turns that could shift cargo.</p>
<p>Real-time tracking alerts are sent to the client every 30 minutes, providing transparency and peace of mind. The vehicle is inspected at every fuel stop to ensure tie-downs remain secure and no shifting has occurred during the journey.</p>
